    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19328" root="سدس" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُدُسٌ</span></b>  (S, M, A, Msb, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُدْسٌ</span></b>  (S, Msb,
K) <i>A sixth part;</i> (S, M, A, Msb, K;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدِيسٌ</span></b> , (S, Msb, K,) a form used by some, like
as one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُشْرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشِيرٌ</span>: (S:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْدَاسٌ</span>. (M,
Msb, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence, app., the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَرَبَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْمَاسَهُ فِى أَسْدَاسِهِ</span>, which see expl. voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُمُسٌ</span>.]

